  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This intimate solo performance by Mountain Goats was captured on May 5, 2018, at Sam's Quik Shop in Durham, North Carolina [1]. The recording, titled tMG2018-05-05, features twelve songs with a total runtime of thirty-two minutes [1]. It was taped by Brandon Wheeler and transferred by notasfarwest [1]. The setlist includes rare archival moments, such as the only archived performance of “Sax Rohmer #1 Intro and Guitar Stuff” and “Keep It On Your Mind (Hank Williams)” [1]. Fans will also hear “Sax Rohmer #1” and “So Desperate,” which are bustouts appearing for the first time in eighty-one archived shows [1]. Other tracks include “Southwood Plantation Road,” “Gameshows Touch Our Lives,” “First Few Desperate Hours,” “Love Cuts the Strings,” “Heretic Pride,” and “No Children” [1]. The song “Old College Try” is noted as being cut on the recording [1]. This show is the 259th of 467 in the archive's collection for the performer [2]. The previous archived show took place on April 22, 2018, at Ardmore Music Hall [2]. The uploader describes the event as a solo show [1].",
